# Build context for `crates/appview/Dockerfile`.
#
# BuildKit reads `<dockerfile>.dockerignore` in preference to the context's own
# `.dockerignore`, which is why this exists as a separate file rather than
# edits to the shared one — no other image's context changes.
#
# This image builds from source, so the context needs the Rust workspace, the
# web app and the SDK it depends on. What it does not need is anything already
# built.

# Build output. `target` is the big one — tens of gigabytes in a working
# checkout, and every byte of it would be uploaded to the daemon and then
# ignored, since the build compiles inside the image.
target
**/node_modules
**/dist

.git
.github

# Local state that must never end up in an image: the session database holds
# live OAuth refresh tokens and DPoP private keys.
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal
*.sqlite
*.ddb
*.ddb.wal
.env
.env.*
rocksky-backup.sql

# Other images' definitions, so touching one does not invalidate this context.
Dockerfile
**/Dockerfile
**/Dockerfile.dockerignore
**/docker-compose.yml

.DS_Store
